On Jun 3, 6:10 pm, Haakon Studebaker <hepta...@gmail.com> wrote:
> I have a YANI and I figure I'll give it a shot. Basically apply a cursed
> tool while confused and it will summon a special monster. What files should
> I look at in the source and what examples would be relevant? Magic lamps
> come to mind.

     doapply() in apply.c prompts for the tool and verifies that
the response is something applicable, then calls a tool specific
function to handle the action.  In whichever function is used for
the tool you're dealing with, you'll need to add a check for cursed
state and perform the desired effect.  Several tools already have
different behavior depending or curse or bless state, so there are
examples in that source file.  [Pick-axes cause code in dig.c to
be called, and musical instruments use code in music.c; almost all
other tools are handled in apply.c.]


